; RNAFold Explorer example sequences
; "Synthetic" sequences were designed for this project to demonstrate one
; structural feature each; they are not natural RNAs.
>Simple hairpin (synthetic, proposal slide 5 wild type)
GGGGAAAACCCC
>Slide 5 mutant C12A (synthetic)
GGGGAAAACCCA
>Hairpin with G-U wobble pairs (synthetic)
GGGUGCAAAAGUACCC
>Stem with a single-nucleotide bulge (synthetic)
GGGGAGGGGAAAACCCCCCCC
>Stem with a 2x2 internal loop (synthetic)
GGGGAAGGGGAAAACCCCAACCCC
>Two-hairpin multiloop (synthetic)
GGGCCCAAGCUCGAAAGAGCAAUGGACGAAAGUCCAUAAGGGCCC
>Saccharomyces cerevisiae tRNA-Phe, 76 nt (modified bases written as unmodified A/U/G/C)
GCGGAUUUAGCUCAGUUGGGAGAGCGCCAGACUGAAGAUCUGGAGGUCCUGUGUUCGAUCCACAGAAUUCGCACCA
